      "source": "PIB India",
      "title": "Rail Coach Factory Kapurthala To Roll Out First Rake Of LHB Coaches For Bangladesh Today",
      "url": "https://swarajyamag.com/infrastructure/rail-coach-factory-kapurthala-to-roll-out-first-rake-of-lhb-coaches-for-bangladesh-today",
      "date": "Wed, 12 Aug 2026 19:34:58 IST",
      "content": "Rail Coach Factory Kapurthala To Roll Out First Rake Of LHB Coaches For Bangladesh Today Infrastructure Rail Coach Factory Kapurthala To Roll Out First Rake Of LHB Coaches For Bangladesh Today Swarajya Staff Aug 12, 2026 | Updated 08:46 AM GMT+5:30 Save & read from anywhere! Bookmark stories for easy access on any device or the Swarajya app . Sign In Prefer Prefer RCF Kapurthala rolls out first rake of LHB coaches for Bangladesh (Pic Via PIB) The Rail Coach Factory in Kapurthala, Punjab, is set to roll out its first rake comprising 19 LHB broad-gauge passenger coaches for Bangladesh Railway today (12 August), marking a significant milestone in bilateral railway cooperation. The rake consists of three AC sleeper cars, three AC chair cars, 11 non-AC chair cars and two power cars, all specially customised to meet Bangladesh Railway's operational requirements. The coaches feature several pioneering design modifications developed specifically for LHB-type coaches. The coaches feature reclining chairs with stainless-steel armrests and footrests, CCTV surveillance, passenger alarm systems, partially openable windows, baby care and prayer rooms. For Bangladesh's specific operating conditions, the roofs have been strengthened to withstand additional loads caused by passengers travelling on them during peak periods. This delivery represents the first instalment of a substantial order placed by Bangladesh Railway in 2024 for 200 broad-gauge passenger coaches in seven different variants, valued at Rs 915 crore. The project, financed by the European Investment Bank, will see the new coaches being added to the ageing Bangladesh Railway fleet between June 2026 and December 2027. The order is being executed through RITES Limited, the export arm of Indian Railways. The partnership between RCF Kapurthala and Bangladesh Railway dates back to 2015-16, when the factory successfully supplied 120 LHB broad-gauge passenger coaches to the neighbouring country. Shipments to Bangladesh had been paused following political transitions in Bangladesh, but deliveries are resuming in mid-2026. Today's rollout highlights India's growing capabilities in international coach manufacturing and railway exports. The coaches feature several specialised design modifications, many of which have been developed for the first time for LHB-type coaches, demonstrating the factory's engineering prowess and ability to adapt products for overseas railway operators. Please click here to add Swarajya as your preferred and trusted news source on Google Tags Bangladesh Railway Rail Coach Factory Kapurthala Join our WhatsApp channel - no spam, only sharp analysis Comments ↓ Get Swarajya in your inbox. Subscribe States",
