      "title": "objective of ayush grid - PIB",
      "url": "https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2297709",
      "date": "Wed, 12 Aug 2026 19:35:09 IST",
      "content": "AYUSH OBJECTIVE OF AYUSH GRID प्रविष्टि तिथि: 11 AUG 2026 5:29PM by PIB Delhi The Ayush Grid project, launched by the Ministry of Ayush, has been envisaged as a comprehensive IT backbone for the Ayush sector with the objective of digitizing service delivery and strengthening transparency, efficiency and governance across healthcare, research, education, drug administration, capacity building and medicinal plants. Ministry of Ayush, under the Ayush Grid initiative, has developed Ayush Hospital Management Information System (AHMIS) which is compliant with the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM). The Ayush Grid project serves as the IT backbone of the Ayush sector, driving digital transformation by integrating advanced technologies such as Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning (ML) and others across functional areas i.e. Healthcare, Research & Development, Education & Awareness etc. Under this initiative, twenty-four e-governance platforms have been developed and made accessible across the country. The My Ayush Integrated Services Portal (MAISP), the master portal of the Ministry of Ayush, integrates all Ayush-related applications and services into a unified digital ecosystem. An AI-enabled chatbot (Beta version) has also been deployed to assist visitors and enhance user experience. The portal facilitates citizen-centric access to various services and schemes and enables real-time monitoring and data-driven decision-making. (Details available at: maisp.ayush.gov.in) Similarly, the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM)-compliant Ayush Hospital Management Information System (AHMIS) has been deployed to digitize healthcare delivery and improve the management of Ayush health facilities. The Ayush Anudan Portal has streamlined the submission, processing, approval, and monitoring of funding proposals under various Central Sector Schemes of the Ministry. The AI enabled Ayush Research Portal serves as a centralized digital repository of over 43,000 curated Ayush research publications, facilitating easy access for researchers, practitioners, and policymakers. The Ayush Nivesh Saarthi Portal serves as a dedicated gateway for domestic and international investors in the Ayush sector, providing comprehensive information to promote investment opportunities. The e-Charak portal functions as a virtual marketplace and information platform for the medicinal plants sector, connecting farmers, collectors, buyers, manufacturers, and exporters integrated with AI assistant for resolving user queries. Further digital platforms like Ayurveda Grantha Samuccaya Digital Library, developed by Ayush Grid and Ayush Manuscripts Advanced Repository (AMAR), Showcase of Ayurvedic Historical Imprints (SAHI) and E- Medical Heritage Accession (E-Medha) developed by Central Council for Research in Ayurvedic Sciences (CCRAS), Ministry of Ayush help digitizing the ancient texts and manuscripts. Collectively, all e-governance tools are accessible to everyone and have strengthened service delivery, improved operational efficiency, and enhanced transparency and accountability. This information was given by Union Minister of State (I/C) for Ayush, Shri Prataprao Jadhav in a written reply in Rajya Sabha today. *** SR/SV/SG (रिलीज़ आईडी: 2297709) आगंतुक पटल : 598 इस विज्ञप्ति को इन भाषाओं में पढ़ें: Urdu , हिन्दी AYUSH OBJECTIVE OF AYUSH GRID प्रविष्टि तिथि: 11 AUG 2026 5:29PM by PIB Delhi The Ayush Grid project, launched by the Ministry of Ayush, has been envisaged as a comprehensive IT backbone for the Ayush sector with the objective of digitizing service delivery and strengthening transparency, efficiency and governance across healthcare, research, education, drug administration, capacity building and medicinal plants. Ministry of Ayush, under the Ayush Grid initiative, has developed Ayush Hospital Management Information System (AHMIS) which is compliant with the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM). The Ayush Grid project serves as the IT backbone of the Ayush sector, driving digital transformation by integrating advanced technologies such as Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning (ML) and others across functional areas i.e. Healthcare, Research & Development, Education & Awareness etc. Under this initiative, twenty-four e-governance platforms have been developed and made accessible across the country. The My Ayush Integrated Services Portal (MAISP), the master portal of the Ministry of Ayush, integrates all Ayush-related applications and services into a unified digital ecosystem. An AI-enabled chatbot (Beta version) has also been deployed to assist visitors and enhance user experience. The portal facilitates citizen-centric access to various services and schemes and enables real-time monitoring and data-driven decision-making. (Details available at: maisp.ayush.gov.in) Similarly, the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM)-compliant Ayush Hospital Management Information System (AHMIS) has been deployed to digitize healthcare delivery and improve the management of Ayush health facilities. The Ayush Anudan Portal has streamlined the submission, processing, approval, and monitoring of funding proposals under various Central Sector Schemes of the Ministry. The AI enabled Ayush Research Portal serves as a centralized digital repository of over 43,000 curated Ayush research publications, facilitating easy access for researchers, practitioners, and policymakers. The Ayush Nivesh Saarthi Portal serves as a dedicated gateway for domestic and international investors in the Ayush sector, providing comprehensive information to promote investment opportunities. The e-Charak portal functions as a virtual marketplace and information platform for the medicinal plants sector, connecting farmers, collectors, buyers, manufacturers, and exporters integrated with AI assistant for resolving user queries. Further digital platforms like...",
