      "title": "MeitY and AAERI Launch DigiLocker Linked AAERI Verify for Students Applying to Australia",
      "url": "https://www.telegraphindia.com/amp/edugraph/news/meity-and-aaeri-launch-digilocker-linked-aaeri-verify-for-students-applying-to-australia/cid/2174445",
      "date": "Wed, 12 Aug 2026 19:35:30 IST",
      "content": "MeitY and AAERI Launch DigiLocker Linked AAERI Verify for Students Applying to Australia - Telegraph India Home News Career Campus Global Education 18 Under 18 Workshops Follow us on Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram Advertisement ministry of electronics and information technology (MEITY) ‘AAERI Verify’ Launched: Check How New DigiLocker Platform Will Aid Indian Students Applying to Australia Our Web Correspondent Posted on 11 Aug 2026 13:18 PM PIB Summary The National e-Governance Division (NeGD) under the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY) has joined hands with the Association of Australian Education Representatives in India (AAERI) to introduce ‘AAERI Verify’. This is a digital platform aimed at simplifying the verification of documents submitted by Indian students seeking admission to Australian universities. The National e-Governance Division (NeGD) under the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY) has joined hands with the Association of Australian Education Representatives in India (AAERI) to introduce ‘AAERI Verify’, a digital platform aimed at simplifying the verification of documents submitted by Indian students seeking admission to Australian universities. The platform is integrated with DigiLocker and is designed to facilitate secure, paperless and consent-based authentication of academic, identity and financial documents. AAERI Verify was officially launched during the AAERI Annual Convention held in New Delhi. AAERI Verify functions as a source-authenticated platform for checking the credentials of prospective international students. Its integration with DigiLocker allows applicants to share digitally issued documents directly from authorised sources with participating Australian higher education institutions. The initiative is expected to reduce the need for physical documents and manual verification, while providing universities with access to records whose authenticity can be traced back to the original issuing authorities. The platform introduces a two-stage verification mechanism to replace conventional document-checking procedures. According to MeitY, the first stage involves student verification conducted before the applicant formally begins the university application process. Advertisement The second stage is a sponsor verification that begins after a student receives an admission offer from an Australian university. During this phase, participating institutions can verify the authenticity of financial documents associated with the student's sponsorship or funding arrangements. The two-step system is intended to address both academic and financial verification requirements at appropriate stages of the admissions journey. The platform operates based on explicit consent from the student. Once permission is provided, Australian universities can access digitally signed records through DigiLocker, with the documents being sourced from the authorities that originally issued them. This consent-based approach is intended to provide students with greater control over the sharing of their personal and educational records while enabling institutions to verify documents through trusted digital sources. MeitY said the initiative is expected to strengthen the reliability of the document verification process and reduce the possibility of fraudulent credentials being submitted during applications. By allowing institutions to authenticate records directly through authorised digital sources, AAERI Verify seeks to create a more dependable mechanism for checking documents submitted by Indian students. The launch of AAERI Verify represents an effort to use India's digital public infrastructure to simplify an important part of the international higher education application process. With DigiLocker serving as the underlying digital document-sharing platform, the initiative aims to create a more streamlined pathway for Indian students applying to Australian universities while helping institutions conduct faster and more reliable verification of academic, identity and financial records. Last updated on 11 Aug 2026 01:19 PM ministry of electronics and information technology (MEITY) DigiLocker Australia foreign universities Advertisement Similar stories Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) CBSE Class 12 Compartment Result 2026 Declared; Check Steps to Download Marksheet Her. . . Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan KVS NVS Tier 2 Result 2026 Expected Soon: Check Result Date, Steps and Cut-off Delhi University DU CSAS PG 2026 Spot Round 2 Schedule Announced; Check Dates, Eligibility MCC NEET UG 2026: MCC Releases Supplementary CW List for Delhi Quota, Check Steps Here read next Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) CBSE Class 12 Compartment Result 2026 Declared; Check Steps to Download Marksheet Her. . . Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan KVS NVS Tier 2 Result 2026 Expected Soon: Check Result Date, Steps and Cut-off MCC NEET UG 2026: MCC Releases Supplementary CW List for Delhi Quota, Check Steps Here Delhi University DU CSAS PG 2026 Spot Round 2 Schedule Announced; Check Dates, Eligibility GATE 2027 GATE 2027: IIT Madras Revises Test City Selection Rule; Check Registration Details Public Service Commission Mizoram PSC Postpones Recruitment Exams, Interviews Indefinitely Amid Students’ Pro. . .",
